---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Stat from '../components/Stat.astro';
import BlocChart from '../components/BlocChart.astro';
import { getTrade } from '../lib/sources';

const trade = await getTrade();
const fmt = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-CA');
const growing = trade.partners.filter((p) => p.name !== 'United States' && (p.changePct ?? 0) > 0).length;
const nonUs = trade.partners.filter((p) => p.name !== 'United States');

const description =
  'Canada is not leaving its largest customer. It is widening the base — and the ' +
  'diversification is already measurable in Statistics Canada\'s monthly trade series.';
---
<Base title="The Bloc" description={description} path="/bloc">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <!-- ===== opener ===== -->
    <section class="open">
      <div class="nt-wrap">
        <div class="nt-label">Four · The Bloc</div>
        <hr class="nt-rule" />
        <h1 class="nt-display lg">We are not<br />leaving.<br />We are widening.</h1>
        <p class="nt-lede" style="margin-top:var(--space-4);">
          A country with one customer is a supplier. A country with ten is a market.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== the honest starting point ===== -->
    <section class="nt-light">
      <div class="nt-wrap">
        <div class="nt-label">The starting point</div>
        <hr class="nt-rule" />
        <h2 class="nt-display md" style="max-width:18ch;">
          The United States is still where most of it goes. That is not changing this year.
        </h2>
        <div class="nt-prose">
          <p><strong>No serious argument begins by pretending otherwise.</strong> Roughly {trade.usSharePct.toFixed(0)} per cent of the goods Canada sells to these nine partners cross one border, and American demand is still growing. Anyone selling you a plan that starts with walking away from that is selling you a slower version of the same trap the separation arguments set.</p>
          <p>The question was never whether to keep the American market. It is whether it should be the only one that matters when the terms are set.</p>
          <p>A supplier with one customer does not negotiate. It receives terms and calls them a deal. That is true of a sawmill and it is true of a country, and the arithmetic does not care which.</p>
          <p><strong>So: widen the base. Not instead of the American market. Alongside it.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== the measurement ===== -->
    <section>
      <div class="nt-wrap">
        <div class="nt-label">What is already happening</div>
        <hr class="nt-rule" />
        <h2 class="nt-display md" style="max-width:20ch;">Look at which direction each line is moving.</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:var(--space-3);max-width:56ch;">
          This is not a proposal. It is Statistics Canada's monthly merchandise
          trade series, read this morning. {growing} of the {nonUs.length} non-American
          partners below are growing faster than the American line.
        </p>

        <BlocChart partners={trade.partners} asOf={trade.asOf} />

        <div class="trio">
          <Stat value={`$${fmt.format(Math.round(trade.restOfWorld))}M`} label="Everyone but the U.S."
                note="Monthly merchandise exports to the other eight partners tracked here, combined." />
          <Stat value={`${growing}/${nonUs.length}`} label="Growing faster"
                note="Non-American partners whose year-over-year growth outpaces the American line." />
          <Stat value={`${trade.usSharePct.toFixed(0)}%`} countTo={Math.round(trade.usSharePct)} label="Still goes south"
                note="The honest number. The argument is about the other side of it, not this one." />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== the anchor case ===== -->
    <section class="nt-redfield">
      <div class="nt-wrap">
        <div class="nt-label">The anchor</div>
        <hr class="nt-rule" />
        <h2 class="nt-display md" style="max-width:17ch;">Korea holds the silicon. We hold the power.</h2>
        <div class="nt-prose">
          <p>The clearest version of the trade is not a slogan, it is a circuit. Korea makes the memory the AI economy runs on and does not have the electricity to run it. Canada has the largest clean, dispatchable power fleet in the Western Hemisphere and does not make the silicon.</p>
          <p>Each half is a vulnerability alone. Together they are an industry. That is what a bloc is for — not solidarity, complementarity.</p>
          <p>The paperwork is not hypothetical. Canada and Korea signed a Security and Defence Cooperation Partnership in late 2025, Canada's first in the Indo-Pacific, and held a second "2+2" ministerial in Ottawa in early 2026.</p>
          <p><strong>This is the part worth repeating: we are not asking for a favour. We are bringing something nobody else in the alliance has in this quantity.</strong></p>
        </div>
        <p class="more">
          <a href="/read/the-closed-loop">Read the full case · The Closed Loop →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== the principle ===== -->
    <section class="nt-light">
      <div class="nt-wrap">
        <div class="nt-label">The principle</div>
        <hr class="nt-rule" />
        <ul class="creed">
          <li class="rv">A country with one customer is a supplier.</li>
          <li class="rv">A country with ten is a market.</li>
          <li class="rv">You do not widen the base out of anger. You widen it because narrow is fragile.</li>
          <li class="rv">Nothing here is taken from a neighbour. It is added beside them.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .open { padding-block: clamp(70px, 13vh, 180px); }
  .open h1 { max-width: 14ch; }
  .trio {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--gap-grid); margin-top: clamp(44px, 7vh, 90px);
  }
  .more { margin-top: clamp(26px, 4vh, 46px); }
  .more a {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px;
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: var(--fw-label);
    font-size: var(--type-label); letter-spacing: var(--ls-key);
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--nt-white); text-underline-offset: 5px;
  }
  .creed { list-style: none; margin-top: var(--space-4); padding: 0; }
  .creed li {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: var(--fw-display);
    text-transform: uppercase; font-size: clamp(19px, 2.5vw, 36px); line-height: 1.1;
    padding: clamp(18px, 2.4vh, 30px) 0; max-width: 26ch;
    border-bottom: var(--border-hair) solid var(--border-hairline);
  }
  .creed li:first-child { border-top: var(--border-hair) solid var(--border-hairline); }
</style>
